List-based (mergeable, multi-value)
===================================

Allow                       = method                                            *(repeat)                         CSV
Connection                  = connection-option                                 *(repeat)                         CSV
Content-Encoding            = content-coding                                    *(repeat)                         CSV
Content-Language            = language-tag                                      *(repeat)                         CSV
Expect                      = expectation                                       *(repeat)                         CSV

If-Match                    = "*" / entity-tag                                  *(repeat)                         CSV
If-None-Match               = "*" / entity-tag                                  *(repeat)                         CSV

TE                          = t-codings                                         *(repeat)                         CSV
Trailer                     = field-name                                        *(repeat)                         CSV
Upgrade                     = protocol                                          *(repeat)                         CSV
Vary                        = ("*" / field-name )                               *(repeat)                         CSV


🟢 1. Singleton fields (one instance only)
Must appear at most once
Not mergeable

Examples:

Content-Length              = 1*DIGIT                                                                             SINGLETON
Content-Location            = absolute-URI / partial-URI                                                          SINGLETON
Content-Type                = media-type                                                                          SINGLETON
Date                        = HTTP-date                                                                           SINGLETON
ETag                        = entity-tag                                                                          SINGLETON
Host                        = uri-host [ ":" port ]                                                               SINGLETON
Last-Modified               = HTTP-date                                                                           SINGLETON
Referer                     = absolute-URI / partial-URI                                                          SINGLETON

If-Modified-Since           = HTTP-date                                                                           SINGLETON
If-Range                    = entity-tag / HTTP-date                                                              SINGLETON
If-Unmodified-Since         = HTTP-date                                                                           SINGLETON
Retry-After                 = HTTP-date / delay-seconds                                                           SINGLETON



👉 Rule:
If repeated → invalid or undefined behavior


🔵 2. List-based fields (CSV, mergeable)
Allow comma-separated values
Multiple lines can be combined safely

Examples:

Accept
Accept-Encoding
Allow
Cache-Control
Connection
Content-Encoding
Content-Language
If-Match
If-None-Match
TE
Trailer
Upgrade
Vary

🟡 3. Repeatable but NOT comma-mergeable

- Can appear multiple times
- Each instance is independent
- Comma-merging would break semantics

Authentication-Info         = auth-param                                        *(repeat)                         CSV
Proxy-Authentication-Info   = auth-param                                        *(repeat)                         CSV
Proxy-Authenticate          = challenge                                         *(repeat)                         CSV
WWW-Authenticate            = challenge                                         *(repeat)                         CSV
Set-Cookie

🟣 4. Structured single fields with internal repetition
- Only one field instance expected
- But internally contain multiple elements
- Not comma-separated — usually space-separated

Server                      = product                                           *(space + repeat or comment)      CSV   RWS  COMMENT
User-Agent                  = product                                           *(space + repeat or comment)      CSV   RWS  COMMENT





Accept-Ranges               = acceptable-ranges
Content-Range               = range-unit SP ( range-resp / unsatisfied-range )                                    GROUP OF VALUES  
Range                       = ranges-specifier

Authorization               = credentials
Proxy-Authorization         = credentials

IMF-fixdate                 = day-name "," SP date1 SP time-of-day SP GMT                                         GROUP OF VALUES                                             
Via                         = (received-protocol RWS received-by [RWS comment]) *(repeat)                         CSV

Location                    = URI-reference     
URI-reference               = <URI-reference, see [URI], Section 4.1>


Max-Forwards                = 1*DIGIT                                                                             DIGITS ONLY
